Below is a summary of what’s happening and how we’ll fix it, followed by five *SEARCH/REPLACE* edits—one for each of the skeleton components:

1.  Bug scenario & root cause  
    In each of the skeleton components (Checkbox, NumberInput, Select, TextInput and TextArea), the `<label>` is rendered with no text content. DAP flags this because an empty label is not a valid accessible name. Since these skeletons are purely visual placeholders (they’re not real, focusable inputs), the correct fix is to hide those labels from assistive technologies by adding `aria-hidden="true"`.

2.  The fix  
    For each of the five skeleton files, we’ll locate the self-closing `<label>` and add an `aria-hidden="true"` attribute.

